    <bpmn:process id="W_W1226" name="W1226. DC Cross-Dock Operations for Fast-Moving Items &amp; Direct-to-Truck Fulfillment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Inbound vendor shipment arrives at DC dock containing fast-moving items (A-class SKUs) with pending outbound store replenishment orders
Frequency: Daily — cross-dock handles ~30% of DC throughput (by volume of fast-moving items)
Volume: ~180–240 cross-dock pallets/day per DC; ~720–960/day across all 4 DCs
Owner: DC Supervisor
Participants: DC Supervisor, Receiving Clerk, Outbound Picker, Forklift Operator, Truck Driver, Supply Planning Analyst
Source: workflow W1226 — DC Cross-Dock Operations for Fast-Moving Items &amp; Direct-to-Truck Fulfillment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1226_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1226_Lane1" name="Supply Planning Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1226_Lane2" name="DC Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1226_Lane3" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1226_Lane4" name="QA Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1226_Lane5" name="Outbound Picker">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1226_Lane6" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1226_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1226_Start8" name="Inbound vendor shipment arrives at DC dock containing fast-moving items (A-class SKUs)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1226_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1226_Task9" name="Cross-dock planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Cross-dock planning (day before): Supply Planning Analyst identifies cross-dock opportunities: (a) match inbound vendor PO expected receipts with pending outbound store replenishment orders, (b) identify A-class SKUs in both inbound and outbound queues, (c) generate cross-dock allocation: which inbound pallets → which outbound trucks → which stores, (d) send cross-dock plan to DC Supervisor with allocation details
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1226_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1226_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1226_Task10" name="Dock door assignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Dock door assignment: DC Supervisor assigns dedicated cross-dock doors: (a) inbound vendor truck assigned to door on one side of cross-dock zone, (b) outbound store delivery trucks assigned to doors on opposite side, (c) cross-dock zone clearly marked with floor tape and signage; no storage shelving in zone — open staging area only
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1226_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1226_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1226_Task11" name="Inbound receiving and sort">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Inbound receiving and sort: Receiving Clerk processes inbound shipment: (a) scan each pallet/case against PO (per W109 goods receipt), (b) identify cross-dock designated items from system (system highlights cross-dock SKUs in receiving screen with destination truck/store assignment), (c) Forklift Operator moves cross-dock items directly to assigned outbound staging lane — no putaway to storage locations, (d) system updates: goods receipt posted, inventory allocated to outbound shipment (inventory in transit for &lt; 4 hours)
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Forklift Operator
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 2–4 hours per inbound truck</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1226_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1226_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1226_Task12" name="Quality check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quality check (if required): for cross-dock items requiring QC inspection (e.g., new vendor first shipment, items with quality history): QA Inspector performs quick inspection at cross-dock staging lane before releasing to outbound truck; if fail: item moves to quarantine per W219, not cross-docked
Responsible (R): QA Inspector (if needed)
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min per check</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1226_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1226_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1226_Task13" name="Outbound loading">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Outbound loading: once outbound truck is fully staged (cross-dock items + regular picked items): (a) Outbound Picker and Forklift Operator load truck per load plan (heavy items on bottom, fragile items on top per W106), (b) verify load against outbound shipment manifest, (c) seal truck; Driver signs dispatch documents
Responsible (R): Outbound Picker / Forklift Operator
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 1–2 hours per truck</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1226_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1226_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1226_Task14" name="System reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: System reconciliation: system reconciles cross-dock flow: (a) goods receipt (inbound) → inventory allocation → dispatch confirmation (outbound) with timestamps; (b) cross-dock items should show &lt; 4 hours dwell time in system; (c) any discrepancies (received quantity ≠ cross-docked + stored quantity) flagged for DC Supervisor investigation
Responsible (R): System / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: Automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1226_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1226_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1226_Task15" name="Daily cross-dock performance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Daily cross-dock performance tracking: DC Supervisor reviews daily cross-dock metrics: (a) cross-dock volume (pallets/cases) as % of total outbound, (b) average dwell time (target: &lt; 4 hours from receipt to dispatch), (c) cross-dock accuracy (correct store assignment), (d) dock door utilization during peak hours
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1226_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1226_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1226_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1226_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1226_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-251 (ensure controlled execution — DC Outbound Operations (PA-04.2).) | - operational: DC Supervisor review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: DC Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
