    <bpmn:process id="W_W1368" name="W1368. DC Store Replenishment Wave Planning, Release &amp; Prioritization Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily outbound planning cycle starts at DC; replenishment orders (auto-generated per W4) ready for processing; or priority store request (stockout risk, promotional launch)
Frequency: Daily per DC; morning planning cycle starts at 5:00 AM for same-day dispatch
Volume: ~12,500 replenishment orders/DC/month (50,000 total across 4 DCs, production-calibrated per data-volumes §1.1); ~415–425 orders processed per DC per day
Owner: DC Dispatch Coordinator
Participants: DC Dispatch Coordinator, DC Manager, Supply Planner, Store Manager (priority requests)
Source: workflow W1368 — DC Store Replenishment Wave Planning, Release &amp; Prioritization Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1368_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1368_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1368_Lane2" name="DC Dispatch Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1368_Lane3" name="Supply Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1368_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1368_Start5" name="Daily outbound planning cycle starts at DC; replenishment orders (auto-generated per W4)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1368_Task6" name="System aggregates all pending replenishment orders for the DC: auto-generated…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System aggregates all pending replenishment orders for the DC: auto-generated orders from W4 (ROP-triggered), manual override orders from W596, priority rush orders from stores, and promotional pre-position orders from W1257
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): DC Dispatch Coordinator
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1368_Task7" name="DC Dispatch Coordinator reviews pending order queue: filters by delivery region…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: DC Dispatch Coordinator reviews pending order queue: filters by delivery region (stores grouped by geographic zone), priority flag, requested delivery date, and order size
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch Coordinator
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1368_Task8" name="System proposes wave plan: (a) groups orders by delivery region (each DC serves…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System proposes wave plan: (a) groups orders by delivery region (each DC serves ~50 stores grouped into 8–12 delivery zones); (b) within each zone, sequences orders by delivery window (morning vs. afternoon); (c) allocates orders to truck capacity (10-wheeler: ~20–25 pallets; 6-wheeler: ~10–15 pallets); (d) identifies multi-drop route potential (2–3 store drops per truck per W106); (e) flags any orders exceeding standard truck capacity requiring special transport (lumber, steel bar, bulk cement)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1368_Task9" name="DC Dispatch Coordinator reviews system-proposed wave plan and adjusts: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: DC Dispatch Coordinator reviews system-proposed wave plan and adjusts: (a) promotes priority orders (stockout-risk stores, promotional launches) to earlier waves; (b) consolidates small orders from the same zone into combined shipments; (c) splits oversized orders across multiple trucks or defers non-urgent lines to next wave; (d) confirms wave sequence aligns with dock door availability per W1353
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch Coordinator
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1368_Task10" name="DC Dispatch Coordinator releases first wave to warehouse floor: system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: DC Dispatch Coordinator releases first wave to warehouse floor: system generates pick lists (RF-directed) for released orders; wave status set to &quot;Released&quot;; subsequent waves remain in &quot;Planned&quot; status pending release
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch Coordinator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1368_Task11" name="DC Dispatch Coordinator monitors wave execution progress: tracks pick…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: DC Dispatch Coordinator monitors wave execution progress: tracks pick completion rate, staging status, and loading status per W1353; releases next wave when current wave is 70–80% picked to maintain continuous workflow
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch Coordinator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1368_Task12" name="If store requests priority rush order (stockout on a top-selling item, customer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: If store requests priority rush order (stockout on a top-selling item, customer special order urgency): (a) Store Manager contacts Supply Planner; (b) Supply Planner authorizes rush replenishment and flags order as &quot;Priority Rush&quot; in system; (c) DC Dispatch Coordinator inserts rush order into current or next wave, bumping lowest-priority order to following wave; (d) system notifies bumped store of revised delivery date
Responsible (R): Supply Planner / DC Dispatch Coordinator
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 15 min/rush order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1368_Task13" name="End of planning cycle: DC Dispatch Coordinator runs daily wave performance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: End of planning cycle: DC Dispatch Coordinator runs daily wave performance summary — waves planned vs. waves released vs. waves dispatched on time; identifies orders deferred to next day; documents reasons for deferral (capacity constraint, carrier no-show, inventory shortage)
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch Coordinator
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1368_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1368_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1368_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1368_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-251 (ensure controlled execution — DC Outbound Operations (PA-04.2).) | - operational: DC Dispatch Coordinator review and approval gate
Owner: DC Dispatch Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
