    <bpmn:process id="W_W1415" name="W1415. New Store Pre-Opening Merchandise Loading, DC Allocation &amp; Initial Stock Build Execution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store go-live date confirmed (typically 4–6 weeks before opening); triggered by VP Store Operations confirming store construction completion and target opening date
Frequency: 10–15 new stores/year (~1–2 per month during expansion phases)
Volume: ~35,000 SKUs × 1 new store = ~35,000 allocation lines per store opening; average initial stock value of ~PHP 25–40M per store
Owner: Supply Planning Manager
Participants: Supply Planning Manager, DC Supervisor, Category Manager, Merchandise Planner, Store Manager (new store), Logistics Coordinator, FP&amp;A Analyst
Source: workflow W1415 — New Store Pre-Opening Merchandise Loading, DC Allocation &amp; Initial Stock Build Execution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1415_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1415_Lane1" name="Supply Planning Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1415_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1415_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1415_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1415_Lane2" name="Logistics Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1415_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1415_Lane3" name="DC Pick Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1415_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1415_Lane4" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1415_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1415_Lane5" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1415_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1415_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1415_Start7" name="New store go-live date confirmed (typically 4–6 weeks before opening); triggered by VP…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1415_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1415_Task8" name="Allocation planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Allocation planning (T-6 weeks): Supply Planning Manager generates initial stock allocation for new store: (a) system creates allocation proposal based on planogram (full assortment depth by category), (b) each SKU allocated at 2–4 weeks of projected demand (A-items at 4 weeks, B-items at 3 weeks, C-items at 2 weeks), (c) Category Managers review and adjust allocations for local market conditions (e.g., Visayas stores need more typhoon-related items, Mindanao stores need more garden/outdoor), (d) total allocation reviewed against merchandise budget (PHP 25–40M) with FP&amp;A Analyst
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1415_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1415_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1415_Task9" name="DC capacity and inventory check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: DC capacity and inventory check (T-5 weeks): (a) system checks available inventory at assigned DC for all allocated SKUs, (b) identify shortfalls: items where DC stock is insufficient for initial load + ongoing replenishment to existing stores, (c) for shortfall items: trigger expedited POs or inter-DC transfers per W22/W1423, (d) DC Supervisor confirms staging area availability (new store loads require 200–400 pallet positions of staging space over 2–3 weeks)
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1415_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1415_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1415_Task10" name="Staggered dispatch planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Staggered dispatch planning (T-3 weeks): (a) Logistics Coordinator creates dispatch plan: divide allocation into 15–25 truckloads over 5–7 delivery days, (b) prioritize by category: lumber/building materials first (outdoor yard setup), then heavy/bulky items (racking placement), then shelved items, (c) schedule 2–3 trucks per day to avoid overwhelming new store receiving dock, (d) assign trucks and drivers per fleet plan per W52
Responsible (R): Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1415_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1415_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1415_Task11" name="DC pick, stage and load">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: DC pick, stage and load (T-3 to T-1 weeks): (a) DC pick staff pick allocated items from forward-pick and reserve locations, (b) staged by truckload in outbound staging area labeled with new store code, (c) DC Supervisor verifies completeness per truckload against allocation list, (d) load outbound trucks per W106 dispatch procedures
Responsible (R): DC Pick Staff / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 weeks (concurrent with other DC operations)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1415_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1415_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1415_Task12" name="Store receiving and putaway">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Store receiving and putaway (T-1 week to Day 0): (a) new store receiving team processes inbound per W109, (b) Stock Associates and Store Manager direct putaway to planogram locations, (c) system updated with goods receipt and bin assignments, (d) Store Manager conducts shelf-fill walkthrough to verify completeness before opening day
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Stock Associate / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–7 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1415_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1415_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1415_Task13" name="Post-load inventory verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-load inventory verification (Day 0–1): (a) Store Manager conducts full walkthrough to verify all planogram locations are stocked, (b) system generates initial stock-on-hand report for new store, (c) Supply Planning Manager compares actual loaded quantities vs. allocation: identify gaps, (d) emergency replenishment orders placed for critical gaps (must-fill items for opening day)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1415_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1415_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1415_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1415_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1415_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-251 (ensure controlled execution — DC Outbound Operations (PA-04.2).) | - operational: Supply Planning Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Supply Planning Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
